From d9fec4746628c72ebb5db7c245adac2e33e89888 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Raimondas Lencevicius <59739769+raimondasl@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:33:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03/18] Validate and record request.service_tier

The Google Interactions and OpenAI adapters already forward request-block
keys as SDK keyword arguments, so `service_tier` reached the provider, but
nothing checked the value or recorded which tier served each step.

- Config loading validates request.service_tier against the pinned SDK
  literals: google-genai interactions {flex, standard, priority};
  openai responses and chat_completions {auto, default, flex, scale,
  priority}. Unset stays unset (provider default).
- ModelResponse.service_tier carries the tier the provider reports.
- Step records store it as `service_tier`; run_meta.json stores the
  configured `requested_service_tier`. Both are omitted when absent, so
  legacy artifacts are unchanged.
- A reported tier that differs from an explicit request (not `auto`) is
  logged as a warning.

Tests use the real SDK clients over httpx.MockTransport, including the
continuous-conversation and harness-summary compaction requests.

